# P114 on iOS (UIKitBackend): the left-edge swipe follows the finger and completes or cancels on release, as UINavigationController's does.
# Steps: push Fruits and Untitled (depth 2). A slow drag to x 120 held still before release: cancelled (the screen slides back; the stack reports a pop and the push that restores it). A slow drag to x 300 held still: past half the 440-point width, completed (depth 1). A short fast throw: completed by speed (depth 0).
# Pass: the replay reports replayed; the log shows depths 1 2 1 2 1 0 in that order; the final capture shows the Home screen with no back control. Screenshots taken during the holds show the popped screen moved right over the previous one.
